"""Labelled detection datasets for the adaptation contract: the digest-pinned BCCD blood-cell sample, the record
contract and its structural validation, image-disjoint splitting, and the BYOD loader.

A record is ``{id, image, boxes, labels}`` where ``image`` is a PIL image (sides within the pipeline's ceilings),
``boxes`` a list of ``[x0, y0, x1, y1]`` pixel boxes inside it (at least one) and ``labels`` one phrase per box drawn
from the dataset's prompt vocabulary — the phrases the detector is asked to ground. The vocabulary is passed beside the
records (``prompts``) and doubles as the per-category breakdown.

The default sample is the BCCD blood-cell dataset (Shenggan/BCCD_Dataset, **MIT**): 364 microscope photographs of
blood smears, 640x480, with 4,886 boxes over three classes (red blood cells, white blood cells, platelets; two zero-area boxes in the
source annotations are dropped), read from GitHub at an immutable commit. Every image is pinned by byte size and SHA-256 and fetched from the raw-content host at
run time; the boxes (from the repository's Pascal VOC annotations at the same commit) travel inline in
``SAMPLE_IMAGES``. The classes are spelled out as the phrases the detector is prompted with (``PROMPTS``).
"""
# ruff: noqa: E501  -- record and pin literals are kept on single lines

